      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I tried these.\n-Delete the Library folder and re-import everything.\n-Upload the SDK back to the version that was uploaded correctly in Unity 2018\n・ Obtain a new BluePrint ID\n-Duplicate Scene file\nThere are no red errors on the console.\nImmediately after the Build is finished, the dialog \"The following open scene have been changed on Do you want to reload the scene?\" Always appears.\nThe Scene file has not been updated externally.\nThis will bring up the same dialog for other projects.\nThe Upload seek bar is getting an error at about the same position every time.\nProjects with a small world size don't have this problem, but uploads are similarly 4-5 times slower than Unity 2018.\nIs the partition that stores the worlds of Unity 2019 limiting the uploaded world size?\nWill it time out if the upload takes too long?\nI'm having a problem because I can't debug the world of Unity 2019. Help me.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
