      "value": "@{5c1475afb7ce126e9e0e3a39|full_name}: Nice catch!\nAlthough there's no difference between 2018 and 2019 this is a good find. We're investigating potential bad side effects but it looks like this will be changed in the next 2019 SDK we add. In the meantime I don't think there's any reason to tell people not to use your example script as a temporary fix.\n@{5b99d19aee038460c535199e|full_name} I will be marking this as \"in progress\" and link to bd_'s post.",
